Warewulf's NetworkManager overlay configures the interface on each node from a
second network device, `roce`:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Optionally configure the RoCE network on compute nodes -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_roce -->
<!-- ohpc_if [[ -n "${roce_dev}" ]] -->
```bash
for ((i=0; i<num_computes; i++)) ; do
	wwctl node set --yes "${c_name[$i]}" --netname=roce --type=ethernet \
		--netdev="${roce_dev}" --ipaddr="${c_roce[$i]}" \
		--netmask="${roce_netmask}"
done
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
